# Raw sources (L3)

OpenShelf's third tier is where you verify or extend a page. This KB's list of
record is the upstream repository
[hexsecs/awesome-automotive-security](https://github.com/hexsecs/awesome-automotive-security),
so the raw material has two homes:

- **The source list** — `README.md` at the pinned `source_commit` in each page's
  frontmatter. `tools/ingest.py` reads it; it is not copied into this directory.
- **The cited evidence** — the `sources:` URLs on every page, which point to
  the papers, documentation and blog posts the page is built from. Concept
  pages cite the entity pages and papers their synthesis rests on.

This directory is the local staging area for material that needs to be kept
verbatim: downloaded PDFs, HTML captures, datasets or logs that a page relies
on and that might otherwise disappear. Nothing is required to be here today.
Add a file here only when a page needs a durable, checkable local copy — and
record it in that page's `sources:` block with a relative path.

Never put derived prose here. Pages go in `wiki/`; this directory is evidence.
